# Line endings for frontend/ only.
#
# Scoped here rather than at the git root because 33-polyglot-monorepo-integration.md's
# boundary rule applies to configuration as much as to code: the frontend's settings must
# not reach backend/, automation/ or infrastructure/. The root .gitattributes already
# carries the repo-wide rules and is NOT replaced by this file.
#
# NOTE ON THE REASON, because the runbook records a different one:
# steps-for-new-repo.md 5.1 justifies this file with "a submodule does not inherit the
# parent's". That premise is false here — RESTRUCTURE-BASELINE.md established that
# frontend/ is an ordinary directory in a single git repository, so it DOES inherit the
# root file. This file exists for the boundary reason above, and because the root's
# `* text=auto` lacks `eol=lf` (14-code-style-and-linting.md requires it, and a
# `prettier --check`-class gate is unsatisfiable on a CRLF checkout without it).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must be re-declared HERE.
# A .gitattributes in a subdirectory takes precedence over the root for files beneath it,
# so the bare `*` line above would otherwise override the root's `*.png binary` for
# everything in frontend/ — including .fidelity/ (91 tracked PNGs, 11.3 MB) and the
# vendored TTF fonts (8.67 MB). `text=auto` does auto-detect binary content, but the
# fidelity captures are the acceptance test for the Phase 2 workspace split and are not
# worth resting on auto-detection.
#
# The fonts are pinned explicitly because the ROOT FILE DOES NOT PIN THEM — it lists
# png/jpg/gif/ico/jar/zip/pdf and no font formats, so *.ttf is `text: auto` today.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
